# Example DNP3 link frames for the dnp3-dpi decoder.
#
# Each line is one hex-encoded link frame with valid CRC-16/DNP header and
# data-block checksums. User data longer than 16 octets is split into blocks,
# each followed by its own CRC.

# Confirmed user data (link function 3, control 0x53): Direct Operate
# (application function 5) on binary-output control group 12, variation 1,
# qualifier 0x17 (8-bit count with 8-bit index prefixes), point 7, control code
# 3 (LATCH_ON). The 18-octet user data spans two CRC-protected blocks, from
# link address 3 to address 1.
0564175301000300a0b8c0c0050c01170107030100000000000069d80000ffff

# Unconfirmed user data (link function 4, control 0x44): Disable Unsolicited
# (application function 21) from link address 3 to address 1.
056408440100030003c7c0c0157ecb

# Unconfirmed user data (link function 4, control 0x44): Cold Restart
# (application function 13) from link address 3 to address 1. The application
# PDU has no object header, so the decoder must not invent one.
056408440100030003c7c0c00d9c86

# Secondary LINK_STATUS (link function 11, control 0x8B) from link address 1
# to address 3. It has no transport or application layer, so it produces no
# JSON event but exercises the corrected link-function name.
0564058b030001008f9b
